{{High Risk|Template:Lowercase|nocat=1|pagetype=Main}}
Forces the '''first letter''' of the displayed page title to lowercase, using <code><nowiki>{{DISPLAYTITLE:}}</nowiki></code>. MediaWiki capitalizes the first character of every page name, so this is the fix for stylized names that are properly lowercase — for example <code>kradness</code> or <code>nqrse</code>. The namespace prefix is preserved. Takes no parameters.

Place it anywhere on the page; the top is conventional.

==Syntax==
{{T|Lowercase}}

==Usage==
This template is shown as code only — a live call would change the title of this documentation page.
<pre>
{{Lowercase}}
</pre>
On a page named <code>Nqrse</code>, the title displays as <code>nqrse</code>.

==See also==
* {{T|Pagetype}} — returns a noun for the current page's type